+## Usage reported to afterModelResponse
+
+`afterModelResponse` is the hook a deployer reaches for when they need to record what a turn cost — an audit entry, a billing line, a usage budget — so the usage it hands over covers the turn, not the final provider call alone (re-cinq/HALEngine#93). One argument carries both: the numeric fields are the per-field sum across every round that reported, and `rounds` lists each reporting round's usage in call order, present only when more than one round reported so that a turn with a single reporting round — the no-tool path among them — receives exactly the usage it always did. The two shapes the issue weighed were folded rather than chosen between: a wrapper object for the third argument was rejected because it would move what the no-tool path receives, and a bare re-typed sum was rejected because the signature would still not say whether the number is a total.
+
+- A turn driven through two tool rounds reports usage covering every provider call in the turn: the per-field sum of the rounds' reported usage, plus the rounds' usage in call order ([validated by: reports a turn total across two tool rounds, not only the last round](../../src/orchestration/turnUsage.acceptance.test.ts#L63)).
+- A round that reports no usage is skipped rather than summed, so the rounds that did report are still counted and neither `undefined` nor `NaN` reaches the hook; the breakdown lists each reporting round in call order ([validated by: counts only the rounds that reported when a provider omits usage mid-turn](../../src/orchestration/turnUsage.acceptance.test.ts#L89)).
+- A turn in which no round reported usage still reports nothing: the hook receives `undefined`, not a zeroed or NaN total ([validated by: still reports nothing when no round in the turn reported usage](../../src/orchestration/turnUsage.acceptance.test.ts#L119)).
+- A turn with a single provider call — a question answered with no tools — reports exactly that call's usage ([validated by: receives collected response text and usage](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L236)).
+
 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
-These two properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` are recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue changes none of them; each is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
